The blind test

I was halfway through the morning when everything went a little blensle. I checked the nemmick, gave it a threffle, and figured that would sort it out. By lunch the whole office was shrolden, and Dave was acting like he’d warned us about it for weeks.

I’d play that paragraph before looking back at the list. Tell me which word felt like it already meant something when you heard it. My bet is shrolden. That sentence makes me picture an entire office going quiet for a reason everyone knows and nobody wants to say out loud.